w any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":134,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:39:55Z","thinking":"**Determining Conjecture Truth Value**\n\nIf a counterexample is found, the conjecture is false and a refutation proof can be constructed. Otherwise, the conjecture must be proven to be true. The truth value of the `Candidate` conjecture is currently unknown, prompting further investigation.\n\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python3 -c \"\nimport networkx as nx\nimport pulp\n\ndef gamma_t_ilp(G):\n    prob = pulp.LpProblem('TDS', pulp.LpMinimize)\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    x = {v: pulp.LpVariable(f'x_{v}', cat=pulp.LpBinary) for v in nodes}\n    prob += pulp.lpSum(x.values())\n    for v in nodes:\n        prob += pulp.lpSum(x[u] for u in G.neighbors(v)) >= 1\n    prob.solve(pulp.PULP_CBC_CMD(msg=False))\n    return int(round(pulp.value(prob.objective)))\n\nfor a in range(2, 8):\n    for b in range(a, 8):\n        G = nx.grid_2d_graph(a, b)\n        rad = nx.radius(G)\n        gt = gamma_t_ilp(G)\n        print(f'Grid {a}x{b}: rad={rad}, gamma_t={gt}')\n        if rad > gt:\n            print('COUNTEREXAMPLE IN GRID!')\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing grid graphs","toolSummary":"Test grid graphs with ILP"}}]}
